1. THE FINDING AND THE CASE (RECORD)
   L8P-R10-F1 (record l8p round 10, l8p_rowc.out 3a, computed again here by l8p_rowc.py): at the breaker's held 23.93 A from 76.25 C the three
     25 A MINI blades (P's F1, E's F3, A's F1; Littelfuse 297) carry 103.6 % of their printed rerated current (23.10 A at the air, 22.75 A at the
     band's 85.41 C): OVER by 0.83 A; the 18 A service is 77.9 % of it: within
   the case: C-PROT rev 1 (the breaker's band 18.32 to 23.93 A held from 76.25 C, board P's FETs welded, no firmware, 10 A held and 18 A for 60 s
     never interrupted; record l9stk's condition C4: an indicated 18 A may be a true 18.80 A)
   what may not move (the brief, constitution 4): no protection lowered, not the 18 A service, no printed rating's margin

2. THREE APPROACHES ON PRINTED FIGURES (constitution section 4: at most three, materially different)
   (A) A FUSE OR A HOLDER ARRANGEMENT THAT CARRIES 23.93 A ON ITS PRINTED RERATING
     a 25 A element needs a printed rerating of at least 0.9572 at 76.25 C (and at the band's 85.41 C); the held MINI 297 prints 0.9238 and 0.9099
       (READING of its line); no other maker's sheet held or read prints a 25 A element at or above it: NOT AVAILABLE ON PRINTED FIGURES
     a 30 A element (0297030) carries it on its own row (27.71 A rerated at the air), but the copper was sized and coordinated at the 25 A
       blade (record l9stk 14.4 to 14.6): the 30 A blade's 135 % to 200 % band runs from 40.50 A to 60 A for up to 600 s, and the bands'
       steady reading at 60 A, scaled by the current squared from the record's own 50 A row (116.60 C), is 134.4 C over board A's 125 C and
       board E's 120 C with the plating pinned: a protection lowered: REFUSED (round 10's (a)); the copper's weight is the open OWNER
       DECISION (L9STK CU), not this record's to move
     a holder or busbar that cools the blade: Littelfuse's rerating curve is drawn against the AMBIENT temperature (READING of its axis);
       no printed figure of the 297 sheet or the 3568's credits a holder or busbar with a lower blade temperature, and the 76.25 C air
       is every blade's ambient inside the sealed case: NO PRINTED BASIS
     verdict (A): NOT SUPPORTED on printed figures
   (B) A HELD-OVERCURRENT TRIP ON BOARD P THAT ENDS IN THE -1'S OWN LATCH (apply_gen_sch_p_ocheld.py; section 4)
     the held current is ended over a window of 19.96 to 21.52 A (printed maxima; R10 as the record assumes it, E-6), inside 18.80 A (the
       service's true current, C4) and 22.75 A (the blades at the band); above it a single event per recovery, the -1's own
     verdict (B): SUPPORTED on printed figures, CONDITIONAL as section 4 names
   (C) A CONTROLLER WITH A TIGHTER PRINTED CURRENT-LIMIT SPREAD (TI LM5066I, SNVS950C, the record's E-5 fallback)
     its VCL at CL = GND 45 to 55 mV (PRINTED, -40 to 125 C) with RS's window spread 1.0204 (record l9stk 15.4): the least kept at 18.32 A
       gives a most of 22.85 A: under the air's 23.10 A by 0.25 A, OVER the band's 22.75 A; at the service's true 18.80 A the most is 23.45 A, over both
     its recommended VIN starts at 10.0 V, 0.6 V under the pack's least 10.6 V; and it replaces the whole breaker of record l9stk 15.4 to 15.6
       (its power limit, timer, SOA, latch and the drafts of rounds 1 to 4)
     verdict (C): NOT SELECTED (fails the band reading and C4's service current on printed figures; the largest redesign of the three)

3. THE SELECTION (SESSION, decision L8P-R11-D1): (B)
   why: the one approach that ends every held current under the blades' printed rerated current at both readings without moving the
     breaker, the copper, the 18 A service or any printed margin; it adds a protection and lowers none; every part type is in the kit
   END CONDITION (any one): (1) R10's maker sheet (E-6) reads a tolerance with its temperature coefficient over 130 K outside -7.3 to 8.3 %;
     (2) Layer 6 finds no R140 whose maker prints a single pulse of at least 0.40 J in 1.4 ms; (3) a check of this round finds a held
     current over 22.75 A, a trip at or under 18.80 A, or a crowbar event that does not end in the -1's latch, and a second negative check of
     the same trip follows; then (C) with its band reading resolved, or the blades' evidence route (round 10's (c)) as the supplier's

4. THE TRIP ON PRINTED FIGURES (B)
   4a. THE WINDOW (INFERRED on PRINTED rows; R10 ASSUMED): OCH_A = 19.3 x I x R10 (U106 inverting, R133 over R132); U107's VITP 0.792 to 0.808 V
     (TI SNVSBJ1E 7.5, -40 to 125 C); R132 and R133 at 0.1 % and 25 ppm/K over 100 K; OPA187's VOS 18.8 uV in all (10 uV, 0.015 uV/C over
     100 K, CMRR 126 dB at VCM V-), IB 7.5 nA, U107's ISENSE 100 nA through R135; R10 2 mOhm at 1 % and 75 ppm/K over 130 K (ASSUMED,
     record l8p 12c; no maker's sheet held, E-6): the held current is ended from 19.965 A at the least to 21.521 A at the most
     margins: 1.16 A over the service's true 18.80 A; 1.23 A under the blades' 22.75 A at the band (1.57 A under 23.10 A at the air)
     robustness: the window stays inside both while R10 reads within -7.3 % to +8.3 % (the record assumes +-1.98 %)
     OCH_A in the service: 0.386 V at 10 A, 0.695 V at 18 A, 0.726 V at the true 18.80 A: under the least 0.792 V
   4b. THE DELAYS (TI's Equations 5 and 6, C0G at 5 %; the no-capacitor least not printed, taken 0): the trip's sense delay 0.460 to 0.852 ms,
     longer than E-10's 0.282 ms excursions (record l9stk 15.7: the key-down current's excursions above 18.32 A each under it), so the trip,
     whose least is over 18.32 A, is never more sensitive than the breaker's least unit; the arming's delay after PGD falls 4.60 to 8.36 ms
   4c. THE CROWBAR INTO THE -1'S LATCH: R140 0.39 Ohm and Q111; its own current 26.9 A at 10.6 V, 42.7 A at 16.8 V, 75.6 A at the 29.2 V clamp,
     each over the breaker's most limit 23.93 A WHATEVER THE LOAD: U101 enters its current limit (its circuit breaker from 30.21 A) and the
     fault timer latches the -1 off, clearing 1.292 ms at most from the limit's onset plus tCL (45 us typical, no maximum: RECORD, l9stk
     prot 3): the row 'an overload over the unit's limit' (40.32 W for 1.292 ms against 71.1 W derated: 0.57) and, from 30.21 A, the hot-short
     row's release in 16.5 us; the crowbar's peak with the most limit's load 67.4 A at 16.8 V, 99.6 A at the clamp, under the 116.8 A where VIN to
     SENSE passes its 0.3 V: no row of record l9stk 15.6 is newly reached; ONCE per recovery (redocking, an input's return, the guard's
     cycle: the -1's own); no retry train
     the gate: Q111's Qg(4.5 V) 75 nC at most through R142 from BRK_VIN at 10.6 V: 12.3 us; the event from the held current's onset at most
       2.156 ms (the trip's delay, the gate, the clearing) plus tCL; PGD falls only when VDS passes 1.62 to 3.40 V (RECORD), and the arming's
       least delay after it, 4.60 ms, leaves 3.30 ms for tCL past the gate and the clearing: the crowbar stays until the latch
     R140's single pulse (INFERRED): PACK_P under the limit at most 9.43 V (the most limit through R140 alone), 230 W for 1.292 ms plus 50 us
       of tCL: 0.309 J; the kit's 593 uF on PACK_P from 9.43 V: 0.026 J; the release spike at the clamp: under 0.003 J; at most 0.40 J in all:
       a 2512 part whose maker prints a single pulse of at least that in 1.4 ms (Layer 6; CONDITIONAL, E-6b)
     Q111 (CSD18510Q5B, PRINTED): IDM 400 A against 99.6 A; VDS 40 V against PACK_P's 29.2 V clamp; VGS 20 V against D105's 12.7 V
   4d. THE ARMING AND THE GATE DRIVE (PRINTED limits; leakages ASSUMED to double every 10 K at the record's 86.25 C site)
     Q110 (AO3401A) driven at VGS -3.39 V at 10.6 V to -9.34 V at the clamp (R136 over R137), against its +-12 V and its -2.5 V RDS(on) row
     Q110 held off: RESET1's 300 nA and Q112's off leakage 5.58 uA through R136: 0.277 V, under its least threshold 0.5 V
     the crowbar held off: Q110's off leakage 43.6 uA (5 uA at 55 C PRINTED) through R138: 0.205 V (0.570 V at a 101 C site), under Q111's least
       threshold 1.2 V (25 C row; the threshold falls with temperature, TYPICAL Figure 6: a layout condition keeps both off the pad)
     U107's RESET1 sinks at most 0.199 mA and RESET2 0.029 mA (TI recommends 5 mA); U107's VDD and SENSE at most 29.2 V against 65 V;
       Q112's gate at most 14.6 V against 20 V; OCH_CG under D105's 12.7 V; R142 and D105 carry at most 17.8 mA for the event
   4e. POWER-UP, THE START AND A LATCHED BREAKER: U107 holds RESET1 and RESET2 asserted for tSD (2 ms at most) and RESET2 while PGD is
     low, so Q112 is off and the crowbar disarmed whenever the breaker is not running: at a gauge's wake, at a docking (the RC hold's
     0.110 s and the start), during a start (PGD low while VDS is high) and once latched; the trip touches neither the enable loop nor
     UVLO (check_l8p_och's APART): L4-E11 20c's window, its readings and the RC hold's 0.110 to 0.907 s are unchanged
     EACH SOURCE PRESENT OR ABSENT (C-PROT rev 1): with a source holding VSYS and board A's battery FETs on, the crowbar also loads the
       source through those FETs, CELL+, the dock and the lead, for the event and the crowbar's turn-off after the latch (RESET1's
       release at most 40 us without a capacitor, PRINTED, and R138 with Q111's 11.4 nF: 0.31 ms), 2.46 ms at most; that current returns
       through board A's ground, not R10, so it never holds the trip; board E's entry meets it as a short on VSYS, its overcurrent 6.364 to
       7.136 A and its short-circuit 10.36 to 13.87 A (record l4e11 3c, RECORD), its own fault behaviour, the case its own record judges; the
       battery FETs carry at most that source current, reversed, inside their held rows; afterwards a charge through the latched
       breaker's body diodes is route R1's (round 3: the detector holds the return, board A's inhibit sets), as after any latch
     THE GAUGE: R10 carries the event, so the gauge's AFE reads it as it reads any short on PACK_P (IF-6); its levels are unchanged
       (IF-4), and if its ASCD acts Q2 opens behind the latched breaker; the gauge's recovery is the battery stream's
   4f. THE STANDING CURRENT from BRK_VIN: U106 150 uA, U107 2.6 uA, R139 with R141 8.4 uA at 16.8 V (PRINTED maxima): beside the detector's
     0.47 mA (record l8p round 3), a standby load on the pack for the battery stream
   4g. ITS OWN SINGLE FAILURES (INFERRED from the circuit as drawn):
     U106 or U107 dead, Rin open, RESET1 stuck high       the trip lost, LATENT: round 10's rows (the blades over by 0.83 A)
     Q112, Q110, R142, Q111 or R140 open; D105 short      the crowbar lost, LATENT: as above
     U106's output stuck high, Rf open                    a trip at every running start: the -1 latches, the kit dark (found)
     Q110 or Q111 shorted                                 the crowbar at every start: the -1 latches in its start (found)
     Q112 shorted, RESET2 stuck high                      the arming lost: a crowbar for tSD at a gauge's wake on a live PACK_P
     RESET2 stuck low, C120 shorted                       the crowbar disarmed, LATENT: as the first row
     C119 open                                            the sense delay 17 us at most: a trip on an excursion E-10 allows (found)
     so a latent first failure returns the design to round 10's rows at 23.93 A held (the blades at 103.6 % of their rerated current, no part
       the guard protects exposed: M-A holds the FETs at 23.93 A); no automatic diagnostic is drawn: E-12f at commissioning and at each
       service, and an automatic test is REMAINING ENGINEERING with HO-A's pattern
   4h. A FINDING ON THE DRAWN UVLO NODE (L8P-R11-F1, this record's own C-1b of round 2; OPEN; not this round's circuit, which adds
     nothing on UVLO): below its threshold U101 sinks UVLOHYS, 12 to 30 uA PRINTED, so at a start H settles under R104 with that sink and
     every off leakage on BRK_UVLO; record l9stk counts the sink alone (H 4.60 V at 10.6 V, R104 nominal). Q104's and Q105's drains sit on BRK_UVLO: at
     the 2N7002's 80 nA at 25 C (PRINTED) doubled every 10 K (ASSUMED, the record's own rule), R104 +1 %, D102's 0.715 V and UVLOTH's
     2.55 V (RECORD): at 10.6 V UVLO reaches 2.70 V with both at the 76.25 C air (0.15 V of margin) and 1.57 V at the 86.25 C site: NOT RELEASED;
     the release at the pack's least fails above a site of 78.0 C on that rule: a docking with board P warm and the pack low would not
     start the breaker (the service, not a protection). Smallest corrections, for this record's next round (none drafted here): R104
     lowered with C103 raised to keep the hold's 0.110 to 0.907 s, or inverters whose maker prints the hot off leakage, or both;
     evidence: Q104's and Q105's IDSS at 86.25 and 101 C on board P's specimen (E-12's bench)

